# QFAI's default, seeded by `npx qfai init`. It is written only when this file does
# not exist; an existing .gitattributes is never overwritten.
#
# The rules cover only the paths QFAI owns. A repository-wide `* eol=lf` would
# report every file already committed as CRLF as "all lines changed", so a
# setting meant to keep SSOT diffs readable would produce a large unrelated diff
# instead. Line endings for product code stay the project's own decision.
#
# The SSOT artifacts QFAI writes — the markdown, yaml, json and sql under
# .qfai/ — all ship LF-normalised. The Drift Protocol makes the diff of those
# artifacts the reviewable object, so a checkout or an editor save that flips a
# whole file's line endings turns it into an "all lines changed" diff that
# cannot be reviewed. Pinning the line endings here is what prevents that.
#
# text=auto: git detects binaries itself and leaves them out of the conversion.
#
# Adopting this in an existing repository: attributes do not reach backwards
# through the index. If a protected path is already committed as CRLF, run this
# once after adding this file
#
#     git add --renormalize .qfai
#
# and keep the result as its own commit. The root files this one pins to LF —
# qfai.config.yaml, DESIGN.md, .github/workflows/qfai-validate.yml,
# qfai-tests.yml and qfai-docs.yml — go on the same command line if they too
# were committed as CRLF. Skipping this step only defers the "all lines changed"
# diff to the day one of them is next saved with LF endings.

# The SSOT tree QFAI owns
.qfai/** text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF
.qfai/**/*.bat text eol=crlf
.qfai/**/*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The root artifacts and configuration `npx qfai init` seeds
/qfai.config.yaml text=auto eol=lf
/DESIGN.md text=auto eol=lf
# All three workflows `npx qfai init` seeds, not one of them. Pinning a single file
# leaves the other two to arrive as CRLF on a Windows checkout, where this
# setting's purpose — keeping review diffs free of line-ending noise — would go
# unserved for them.
/.github/workflows/qfai-validate.yml text=auto eol=lf
/.github/workflows/qfai-tests.yml text=auto eol=lf
/.github/workflows/qfai-docs.yml text=auto eol=lf
